  "title": "Süßer die Glocken nie klingen",
  "composer": "Traditional",
  "about": "Süßer die Glocken nie klingen means Never do the bells ring sweeter in German. The theologian and teacher Friedrich Wilhelm Kritzinger wrote the words. Bernhard Brähmig first printed the song in 1860, in his collection Liederstrauß, as Die Weihnachtsglocken. The tune is the folk song Seht, wie die Sonne dort sinket, known in Thuringia since 1841.",
  "funFact": "Older words to the same tune already sang of bells, which may have given Kritzinger his idea.",
